# Core workflow (ALWAYS)

You must follow this workflow at the start and end of every task.

## Start of every task
1) Open and read `CONTINUITY.md`.
2) If the user goal, constraints, or state changed since last run - update `CONTINUITY.md` immediately before doing anything else.
3) Read `docs/PROGRESS.md` to understand the last recorded state.
4) Work only from repository facts. Do not assume missing details.

## During work
- If you make any decision that affects architecture, DB mapping, folder structure, build/run steps, or module boundaries - record it in `CONTINUITY.md` under Key decisions the moment you decide.
- If something is unknown, write it to `Open questions` and mark as `UNCONFIRMED`.

## End of every task
1) Update `CONTINUITY.md` sections: Done, Now, Next, Working set.
2) Update `docs/PROGRESS.md` to match the same status (short, factual).
3) If you changed how to run/build - update `docs/DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md`.

## Non-negotiables
- Commands must be provided for bash (not PowerShell).
- Do not create random .bat/.cmd scripts. If a script is required, place it under `ops/` or `modern/*/scripts/`.
- Preserve traceability: every new feature must point to legacy source (Struts/JSP/DAO) and DB objects (tables/procs/triggers) when relevant.
